Changelog: 21-11-2026 13:33:25

Added. PS5 Turing Screen came from its twin, BC-250 Turing Screen, as it is there (owner, 21-11-2026: "we use the same
app we have built here, refactor will be done on the console developer board"). It shows CPU, GPU, memory, fan and
temperatures on a Turzx USB IPS screen. Three tiles follow what this board reports instead of the twin's: the GPU tile
has no power, the Fan tile shows the duty in percent with the fan's mode (the board reports no RPM), and SoC temp
stands where the twin has VRM temp. Not tried on a board yet: the screen itself, and reading the fan driver's values
every second for hours.
